  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-10-04 from the CSS Overflow 5 Editor's Draft (propdef grammar quoted verbatim: none | [ [ before | after ] || [ links | tabs ] ]), the modes/activation sections, CSSWG PR #13627, the explainer gist, ChromeStatus, BCD, webstatus.dev, and runtime_enabled_features.json5. The two mode keywords get stable child routes (links/, tabs/). Known preserved ambiguities, stated on-page rather than invented: (1) box placement for a bare mode keyword without before/after is not defined in the prose read; (2) pre-154 Chrome's implicit marker focus/role behavior is not described in the sources read; (3) BCD has no links/tabs subfeature yet, so mode compat rows are labelled interim ChromeStatus data. Runtime behavior is source-derived, not executed locally."
